     "text": "shape: (64, 64, 3)\ndtype: uint8\nmin: 0\nmax: 255\nmean R: 127.03\nmean G: 127.03\nmean B: 128.00\n"
    }
   ],
   "source": "import numpy as np\n\n# Setup\nH, W = 64, 64\nimg = np.zeros((H, W, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\nimg[..., 0] = np.linspace(0, 255, W).astype(np.uint8)[None, :]   # R: left-to-right gradient\nimg[..., 1] = np.linspace(0, 255, H).astype(np.uint8)[:, None]   # G: top-to-bottom gradient\nimg[..., 2] = 128                                                  # B: constant\n\n# Task 1: Print shape, dtype, min, max, and mean of each channel\nprint(f\"shape: {img.shape}\")\nprint(f\"dtype: {img.dtype}\")\nprint(f\"min: {img.min()}\")\nprint(f\"max: {img.max()}\")\nchannel_means = img.mean(axis=(0, 1))\nprint(f\"mean R: {channel_means[0]:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"mean G: {channel_means[1]:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"mean B: {channel_means[2]:.2f}\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa519e5c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# Task 2: Grayscale Conversion\nConvert the RGB gradient image to grayscale using luminance weights 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B."
